WEBVTT

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:13.000
Stay focused!

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.910
There's only one week left
until the competition.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.080
Yes!

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.870
Joe's battle is around the corner.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.540
Sekigahara, here we come, indeed!

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.290
"Se"

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.080
"ki"

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:28.830
"ga"

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:29.580
"ha"

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.910
"ro"

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.830
Huh?

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.410
Is there another Sekigahara that day, too?

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:10.910
"The Gymnastics Samurai"

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.660
You're in excellent condition.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.830
Just know that this NHK Cup

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.200
won't be an easy fight.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.870
You'll have to compete against
the top gymnasts of the next generation.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.830
Minamino, too, of course.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:34.330
Face it as if you were a beginner again.

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.330
Got it?

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:37.250
Don't forget what you've set out to do--

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:38.620
Huh?

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:40.660
I'm sorry.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.910
Did you say, "Don't forget the <i>shachihoko</i>?"

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:45.500
Just pick up!

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.540
Will you be home late tonight again?

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:48.450
Yeah.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:51.500
I'm having a meeting
with Amakusa after practice,

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.290
so I might not be home until just before eight.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.120
Got it.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.160
I'll be waiting with dinner ready!

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.790
Rei's coming to see this competition, right?

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:02.250
Yes.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.910
I can't disappoint her, no matter what.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.410
You know...

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.200
I invited my daughter, too.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.950
And this is what happened.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:12.830
"If u gimme lots of money"

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.330
"If u gimme lots of money"

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.330
I...

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.370
"If u gimme lots of money"

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.370
I...?

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:18.000
Can you believe it?!

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.200
She sent that to her father!

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.500
So I replied like this.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:23.750
"I'll up UR allowance nxt month"

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:24.910
"I'll up UR allowance nxt month"

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:24.910
I...

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.040
"I'll up UR allowance nxt month"

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.040
U...

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.580
"I'll up UR allowance nxt month"

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.580
U...?

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.580
Am I too easy on her?

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.700
What do you think?

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:34.000
"Episode 5
'Battling Samurai'"

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.950
"Episode 5
'Battling Samurai'"

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.950
Go... Go... Go...

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.830
"Episode 5
'Battling Samurai'"

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.830
Ah! <i>Godzilla</i>!

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.700
<i>Last Action Hero</i>.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.950
Ro... Ro...

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.200
<i>RoboCop</i>!

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.330
<i>Project A</i>!

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:46.620
"A"?!

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.910
A...

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.450
--"Alien."
--Too bad!

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:50.500
You can't end with "n"!

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.620
No!

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.000
I've lost!

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.660
I win!

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.120
You've picked up a lot, Leo!

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.540
You started living with us in November, right?

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.000
That means it's been half a year!

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.700
Time sure does fly, indeed.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.950
By the way, is something happening on July 5th?

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.790
What?

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:15.330
Oh, that day is actually...

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.410
...my birthday!

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:19.750
Oh? Your birthday?

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:20.750
Yup!

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:23.290
We follow a very important family rule.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:26.830
The whole family spends the day
together on our birthdays.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.250
So that day, Dad will be home all day, too.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.200
It's what Mom decided.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.540
That sounds like a great birthday.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.910
For this year...

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.700
Will you celebrate with us, too?

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:51.830
Huh?

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.830
B-Because you're...

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:58.290
...practically family... right?

00:04:58.290 --> 00:04:59.790
That's why!

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:04.580
Family...?

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.950
I-Is that okay...?

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.330
Of course I will!

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.950
It's a promise, indeed!

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:13.830
Yes!

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.750
It's a promise, indeed!

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.000
Break it, and you're subject to seppuku.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.290
Hara-kiri?!

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:41.000
"NHK Cup"
"The Samurai Will Also Compete"

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.950
"42nd NHK Cup Gymnastics"
"May 30, 2003 (Fri) and May 31, 2003 (Sat)"

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.330
"42nd NHK Cup Gymnastics"
"May 30, 2003 (Fri) and May 31, 2003 (Sat)"

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.330
Under the clear sky, the day has finally come!

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.370
"42nd NHK Cup Gymnastics"
"May 30, 2003 (Fri) and May 31, 2003 (Sat)"

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.370
It's the 42nd NHK Cup!

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:56.290
"42nd NHK Cup Gymnastics"
"May 30, 2003 (Fri) and May 31, 2003 (Sat)"

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:56.290
This year's competition has gained
more attention than usual.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:06:00.200
That is because the next generation
of young gymnasts are competing

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:04.620
to brush away the long years of
recession from the gymnastics world.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:07.910
Where's Jotaro?

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:09.660
Doing his usual thing.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:19.500
All right!

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.290
Huh?

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:25.870
Ah.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:27.830
Oh...

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:28.950
Hey.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.450
Oh?

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:36.910
It's been a while, Jotaro.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.950
Nakanomori!

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.250
Yes, it's been a while.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:45.500
I watched your retirement, no,
retirement retraction press conference.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.700
You always liked to surprise people.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:53.750
It's like when you suddenly announced
your marriage to an actress.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.000
Let go.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.910
Greetings are important...

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.950
...among fellow competitors.

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:02.370
Fellow... you say?

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:08.370
Don't let your shoulders get cold
before the actual competition...

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.830
Tecchan.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.790
Sorry about that.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.290
I'm not the most competent coach.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.750
Not at all...

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.330
He's still young,

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:26.000
but his talents are real.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.450
I believe he'll be a leader
in the gymnastics world

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:31.250
from here on out.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:39.370
Whoa!

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:41.450
So this is Joe's battlefield

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:44.580
of Sekigahara, indeed!

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.160
All right, Leo.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:47.410
"Jotaro Aragaki"

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:51.290
"Jo"

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:51.290
Let's put in our all, too, and root for Dad!

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:54.120
"Jo"

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:54.120
But of course!

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.750
The competitors will now make their entrances.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:04.700
Former Olympic athlete, Takashi Kamimura,
joins us today as a commentator.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.830
Mr. Kamimura, are there any competitors
you're especially curious about?

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:12.290
That would be the young gymnasts
who have been standing out in recent years.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:15.450
First up, we have last year's
third-place winner of the nationals,

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:19.160
Jun Dojima of Hokokukai.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:24.950
We have Shigeru Nishikiori of Rittai University
who placed second in the nationals last year.

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:28.750
And here is Hiroshi Okamachi
of Shirando University.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:31.660
He's the champion of both
last year's nationals and NHK Cup,

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:36.250
and currently stands at the
top of the gymnastics world.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:40.200
However, as a competitor who threatens
his successive championship title,

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:44.450
we cannot forget about
Tetsuo Minamino of Play Sports.

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:48.790
He's popularly known as the
"Bandana Prince" these days.

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:51.950
He's grown drastically in the past year.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:55.870
Even as a high schooler,
his growth is truly impressive

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:58.910
and people are already
calling him the ace of the future.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:03.660
It is likely that these four will be the ones
struggling for victory in this competition.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:06.330
The gymnast who caused a buzz
surrounding his retirement,

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:10.370
Jotaro Aragaki of Yotsuba Sports Club
will also compete this year.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.700
Aragaki, huh?

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:15.950
He's been in a slump these past few years.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:21.290
Based on his performance at last year's
nationals, this will be a hard fight for him.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.080
You've got this, Dad!

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:26.410
Show them your gymnastics, Joe!

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:29.540
Go, Takizawa!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.870
Thirty-six gymnasts are competing
at this year's tournament.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:40.580
They will be divided into groups of six
and will rotate through events.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:45.200
In the first floor event,
ace Okamachi performs first.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.290
He executes a sharp roundoff

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.910
before a double double!

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:54.580
A powerful, highest-difficulty
level-E technique!

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:57.120
His landing was perfect, too!

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:00.950
Okamachi is a gymnast who
performs with great finesse.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:03.290
Each technique is extremely polished

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.290
with a high degree of perfection.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:06.790
Please watch.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:16.290
See how his toes point straight up
at the ceiling during his handstand?

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:18.330
It's truly beautiful.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.790
You don't just compete for the difficulty
of techniques in gymnastics.

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:25.080
The beauty of the posture during execution

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:27.580
is crucial to obtain points, too.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:32.790
A truly magnificent performance from Okamachi.

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:35.160
We can expect a high score.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:36.950
"Floor"

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:38.700
"Floor"

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:38.700
There it is! 9.475!

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.660
"Floor"

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.660
As expected from the reigning champion!

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.580
"Floor"

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.580
A high score at his first event!

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:47.830
The second event is the pommel horse.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.830
"Do"

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.830
Go, Dojima!

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.950
Dojima executes a flair spindle...

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:56.410
...into a level-E combination!

00:10:56.410 --> 00:11:00.120
A truly lively and bold performance!

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:03.660
His pommel horse skills have stood out
since his high school years.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:07.080
He's so talented, he's been called
the "Child of the Pommel Horse."

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:08.410
"Pommel Horse"

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:09.910
"Pommel Horse"

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:09.910
9.425!

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:11.910
"Pommel Horse"

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:11.910
Another high score!

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:14.410
"1st place: Jun Dojima"
"2nd place: Hiroshi Okamachi"
"3rd place: Yusuke Kuwahara"

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:16.870
Take a look over here.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:19.120
Nishikiori is on the still rings.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:21.250
He goes from an L-cross Honma

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:22.870
and pulls up with straight arms
to a Maltese cross.

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:26.000
He safely executes E-level skills!

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:29.870
With still rings, upper-body
muscle strength is crucial.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:32.910
Look at his stability. It's wonderful.

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:35.120
The score should come up soon.

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:36.040
"Still rings"

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:37.370
"Still rings"

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:37.370
9.450!

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:40.700
"Still rings"

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:40.700
Nishikiori scores a 9.450!

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:46.870
In the current standings, a narrow margin
separates Okamachi, Nishikiori and Dojima!

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:50.160
But even those three haven't
been able to reach the top!

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:53.830
Who expected to see this kind of development?

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:55.160
Currently at the top...

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:57.160
"1st place: Tetsuo Minamino"
"2nd place: Hiroshi Okamachi"
"3rd place: Shigeru Nishikiori"

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:57.160
...is Minamino!

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:00.950
The one who stands at the top,
surpassing the reigning champion

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:03.040
is Tetsuo Minamino!

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:07.250
"NHK Cup Preliminaries"
"Minamino Takes Off at 1st Place" "Tetsuo Minamino"

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:10.000
"NHK Cup Preliminaries"
"Minamino Takes Off at 1st Place" "Tetsuo Minamino"

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:10.000
How does it feel to surpass Okamachi,
the reigning champion

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:14.500
"NHK Cup Preliminaries"
"Minamino Takes Off at 1st Place" "Tetsuo Minamino"

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:14.500
and place first after finishing
all six events on the first day?

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.080
"NHK Cup Preliminaries"
"Minamino Takes Off at 1st Place" "Tetsuo Minamino"

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.080
I don't care.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:20.120
Gymnast Minamino currently
stands in first place.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.750
There are other strong players there,

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:22.200
so let's see if he can get through
the second day as well.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:25.700
"15 Jotaro Aragaki Horizontal Bars"

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:25.700
so let's see if he can get through
the second day as well.

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:28.330
You're in 15th place, Joe!

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:32.330
Your performance was great, too, Dad!

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:34.580
You didn't do bad at all!

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.080
That's right, indeed!

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:40.660
Even if you placed really low,
there's no need to feel down!

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.290
It's okay.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.790
This is the best I've felt in years!

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.370
That's what I thought!

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:00.290
So you knew, huh?

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:01.660
--Then!
--Huh?

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:04.950
You'll have to beat 14
competitors at once, indeed!

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:06.410
Huh?

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:09.450
Huh?

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.790
Speaking of comebacks!

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:38.540
No good!

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.410
"42nd NHK Cup Gymnastics"
"May 30, 2003 (Fri) and May 31, 2003 (Sat)"

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:43.870
"42nd NHK Cup Gymnastics"
"May 30, 2003 (Fri) and May 31, 2003 (Sat)"

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:43.870
Three events have finished so far,
and we're currently on the vault.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:44.830
"42nd NHK Cup Gymnastics"
"May 30, 2003 (Fri) and May 31, 2003 (Sat)"

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:44.830
Following the first day's momentum,

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:45.660
"1st place: Tetsuo Minamino" "2nd place: Jun Dojima"
"3rd place: Shoichi Nakano"

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:45.660
Following the first day's momentum,

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.540
"1st place: Tetsuo Minamino" "2nd place: Jun Dojima"
"3rd place: Shoichi Nakano"

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.540
the second day has been filled
with incredible performances.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.870
But nobody can seem to stop Minamino.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:53.830
How will Okamachi do?

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:05.910
Unfortunately, Okamachi hops on his landing.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:11.040
His landing wasn't perfect,
but we can still expect a high score.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:11.910
The score's coming in.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.250
"Vault"

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.830
"Vault"

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.830
9.400!

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.660
"Vault"

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.660
He flaunts a soulful performance,
as if to say he won't give away his title.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:19.250
He flaunts a soulful performance,
as if to say he won't give away his title.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:23.500
Up next is Minamino.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:27.660
Yesterday, he showed us his layout Cuervo
with a single twist on the vault.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:38.160
He stuck it!

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:40.910
Minamino finishes with
an impressive perfect landing!

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:42.500
Let's watch it in slo-mo.

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:47.700
That was the Driggs.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:51.120
It's a higher skill level technique
than the layout Cuervo.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:55.370
He continues to impress
with his high-level techniques!

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:56.290
Let's see his score.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:57.410
"Vault"

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:58.830
"Vault"

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:58.830
9.550!

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:01.910
"Vault"

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:01.910
He has surpassed Okamachi's score!

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:06.540
The higher the difficulty level,
the more likely it is for you to fail.

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:08.450
But he raised it anyway.

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:12.540
What is Minamino's motive to take
such risk when he's at the top...?

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:15.250
We don't exist to him.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:16.620
It's not just us.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.290
It's this whole competition.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:22.410
He's using it to test and see how far he can go.

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:24.500
What a jerk...

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:28.870
We are seeing error after error.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:32.080
They must be feeling the pressure
from Minamino's performance.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.790
It only proves there's something frightening
about his performance this year.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:39.080
I wonder if Dad's okay.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.620
No need to worry about Joe!

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.040
Look at him...

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.080
He's smiling.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:50.620
We have to root for him
with a smile, too, Rachel!

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:52.040
Yeah!

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:56.870
The NHK Cup has been a two-day competition,

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.540
which will come to an end with this final event.

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:04.950
What?

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:06.540
Are you curious?

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:07.870
Not really.

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.160
I heard from Amakusa.

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:13.160
Sounds like you made quite the demand.

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:17.120
Well, today's Jotaro...

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:20.750
Whoops, that has nothing to do with you.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:23.290
That's right. It doesn't matter.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.660
Go as far as you'd like.

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:29.660
Today is undoubtedly your day.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:36.410
Minamino faces the final event,
the horizontal bar.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:39.580
All eyes are focused on his performance,

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:44.080
as if they are anticipating the
moment of the birth of a new ace!

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:52.580
What a giant swing.

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:53.700
That's a Kolman!

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.660
His performance shows
he's not feeling any pressure!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.040
Truly a man with an iron heart!

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:05.450
To win.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:07.120
That's all that matters.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:17.160
Success!

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:20.290
Minamino's performance
was wonderful until the end!

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:31.000
The gymnast who conquered
the 42nd NHK Cup...

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:35.330
...was Tetsuo Minamino!

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:37.370
Based on the NHK Cup results,

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:39.910
the representative members
of the 38th World Championships

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:43.950
to be held in August have been determined.

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:47.330
"38th World Championship Representative Members"

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:47.330
This will be Minamino's
second World Championships.

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:50.000
"38th World Championship Representative Members"

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:50.000
His first was last year.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:55.500
His recent rapid progress may be due to
his experience during that tournament.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:18:00.450
It's possible for one occasion
to trigger impossibly great growth.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:04.330
I lost this time.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:09.200
But, to face the world,
I can't keep losing either.

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:16.370
This year's competition saw quite the upsurge,
which has been rare in recent years.

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:17.410
Yes.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:22.910
The fact that the top-rankers are young
tells me the next era is here.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:28.000
Speaking of top-rankers, Aragaki placed 6th.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:32.000
I believe he finished at 15th on the first day.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.160
It's because the other gymnasts lost points

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:37.750
due to the pressure they felt
from Minamino's performance.

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:41.120
Would you say he was saved by others' mistakes?

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:45.250
No, actually, his performance
was very meticulous.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:46.950
Back in the day, when he was
known as the Samurai,

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:51.000
there was some roughness behind
his dynamic performances.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.450
But I saw none of that this time.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:57.700
His gymnastics has dramatically
changed from preceding years.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:01.580
Oh, Grandma?

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:03.080
Yup, it just ended.

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:05.200
Dad placed 6th!

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:11.950
I'm done, Leo!

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:13.830
Hm?

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.410
Leo?

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:18.830
We finally found you.

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:22.540
Dad!

00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:24.040
Have you seen Leo?

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:24.870
What?

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:26.700
He disappeared suddenly!

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:29.500
I wonder if he got lost...

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:30.830
Leo's...

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:32.080
...right there.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:33.410
What?! Leo?!

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:35.120
Where were you?!

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:38.750
It's my Ninja Art:
The Art of Disappearing, indeed!

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:40.080
What?

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:02.750
"I've set out on a journey
for training, indeed
Leo"

00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:05.500
Huh?

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:06.750
Milk...

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:08.290
Dad!

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:09.330
Look at this!

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:13.580
"I've set out on a journey
for training, indeed
Leo"

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:13.580
"...journey for training..."?

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:16.450
I've checked his room, but he wasn't there!

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:21.080
He must've gone out
to play somewhere, like usual.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:23.330
He did... right?

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.540
So? Have you rested enough?

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:28.540
Yes.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:30.750
I had three full days of rest.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:33.040
Regarding the NHK Cup...

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:36.200
The small flaws you had previously
were pretty much non-existent.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:40.620
You've cleared the task of increasing
the precision of your skills.

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:43.830
Next, we'll tackle the high-level techniques.

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:45.160
The hurdle will be raised,

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:50.790
but if you can't master them,
you won't get to go to Athens next year.

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:51.580
Right now, there are talks about holding
a Japan-China joint training camp.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:55.870
"Notice for Japan-China Joint Training Camp"

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:55.870
Right now, there are talks about holding
a Japan-China joint training camp.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:59.040
You're one of the potential
gymnasts to participate in it.

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:01.750
Really? With China?

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:02.750
That's right.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:08.290
The ultimate Chinese team that placed first
at last year's World Championships.

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:12.790
The objective is to heighten each other's
techniques, each nation with our top gymnasts.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:16.200
China's super-ace,
Liu Longxiang will be there, too.

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:19.750
The champion of the individual all-around event.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:22.160
Even what our new champion,

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:25.080
Minamino, scored at the last competition

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:26.580
isn't comparable to Liu's.

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:30.790
"Notice for Japan-China Joint Training Camp"

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:30.790
I'm sure it'll be helpful for you right now.

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:32.370
When does it start?!

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:35.620
It's from July 1st to the 6th.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:37.000
What?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.120
You busy then?

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:41.700
July...

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:43.120
Right on the mark.

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:44.910
My wish came true.
